WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.970
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed to
do at the Foundation: Dr. Bright is not permitted

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:10.019
to assign the designation “Over 9000”
to any anomalies.

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:14.849
Dr. Bright is to be reminded that first of
all, the SCP Foundation does not track the

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:19.660
“power levels” of any of its anomalies,
as that is a completely subjective notion.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:26.749
Adding “it’s over 9000” to official
Foundation documents is distracting, and confusing,

00:00:26.749 --> 00:00:32.270
particularly when applied to entities like
SCP-999 who have no interest in combat.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.860
Second of all, he should know that joke hasn’t
been relevant in over a decade, he’s embarrassing

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.620
himself and none of the new research assistants
even know what he’s referencing.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.750
Finally, he’s not as good at doing the Vegeta
voice as he thinks he is.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.789
Update your references, Dr. Bright!

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:48.480
You’re better than that!

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.000
…Maybe.

